  "findings": [
    "Holding cache true isolates root ordering: Bf5 first iteration 1814 OFF versus3732 ON (+1918). Previous2577 versus3732 mixed cacheOFF baseline with cacheON+ordering candidate; +1155 is not ordering-only cost.",
    "Bf5 rootNg5 cost1 OFF (stand-pat cutoff after an established alpha) versus1915 ON (full-window first branch); exf6 remains1673 versus1677. A motif can be forcing without being the best move. Moving it first did not establish a better bound and expanded checking exchanges.",
    "The Bf5 ON Ng5→Bxb1→Bxf7+→Kd7→Be6+ branch costs832 qnodes. Be6+ is a new optional quiet check at parent qply3, while the earlier Bxf7+ checking capture and its king evasions are mandatory under the retained policy.",
    "Ng5-preroot ON remainsdepth0; Qe1 takes7191/9999qnodes. Qe1→Be4→Qxe4+→Nce7→Ng5 costs3278; siblingNe5 costs1195. Both fork activations occur at parentqply3, even though the check/capture prelude was already resolved.",
    "Ng5-preroot ON6951/9999qnodes (69.52percent) are under a first optional quiet check introduced after parentqply2.9456/9999 are also below checking captures. Removing checking captures or evasions would conflate cost with correctness; bounded optional activation addresses late new branches while retaining capture chains.",
    "The original critical line Bf5→exf6→Bxb1→Ng5 activates Ng5 at parentqply2 from the original black root andqply1 from the white reply root. A fixed optional activation horizon throughparentqply2 preserves that observed motif and immediate defensive replies; it is still a selective heuristic, not a proof that deeper quiet tactics never matter."
